                <pb facs="0633" n="1263" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg1263"/>

                <head>AN ACT in addition to an act entitled “An act to establish an uniform rule of
                    naturalization, and to repeal the acts heretofore passed on that
                    subject.”</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sec</hi>. 2. <hi rendition="#italic">And be it
                        further enacted</hi>, That when any alien who shall have complied with the
                    first condition specified in the first section of the said original act, and who
                    shall have pursued the directions prescribed in the second section of the said
                    act, may die before he is actually naturalized, the widow and the children of
                    such alien shall be considered as citizens of the United States, and shall be
                    entitled to all rights and privileges as such, upon taking the oaths prescribed
                    by law.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Approved <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1804-03-26">March 26, 1804</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
